"""msx_printer_fonts.py - printer glyph sets, in openMSX's column format.

Four charsets are available. MSX takes priority over FX-80: an MSX prints its
own character ROM glyphs, so `msx` is the default and reproduces what the real
machine put on paper - including the upper region (0x80-0xFF: accented letters,
currency, box drawing, greek), which matches CP437's layout.

    msx      MSX International (Philips NMS8250 BIOS)      <- default
    msx-din  ditto, DIN variant (slashless zero)
    msx-jp   MSX Japanese (Sony HB-F1XV BIOS): katakana at 0xA1-0xDF
    fx80     Epson FX-80 character generator ROM. Period-correct FX-80: the
             high bit selects *italics* rather than a second glyph page, and
             accented letters live at 0x00-0x1F (reachable via ESC R, or via
             the CP437 mapping in msx_printer_escp_render).

Storage follows openMSX's printer font layout: `stride` bytes per character,
byte 0 an attribute and the rest the glyph's columns.

    attribute: bits 6-4 = first column to print in proportional mode
               bits 3-0 = one past the last column
               bit    7 = shift columns left by one (use the top 8 of 9 pins)

A column is a 9-bit vertical slice, bit 8 the top pin and bit 0 the bottom.
"""

